{
  "category": "Iron Armor Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "AGGRON claims an entire mountain as its own territory. It mercilessly beats up anything that violates its environment. This POKéMON vigilantly patrols its territory at all times.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "AGGRON is surprisingly protective of its environment. If its mountain is ravaged by a landslide or a fire, this POKéMON will haul topsoil to the area, plant trees, and beautifully restore its own territory.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its iron horns grow longer a little at a time. They are used to determine the AGGRON’s age. The gouges in its armor are worn with pride as mementos from battles.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "It claims a large mountain as its sole territory. It mercilessly thrashes those that violate its space.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "It claims a large mountain as its sole territory. It mercilessly thrashes those that violate its space.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "While seeking iron for food, it digs tunnels by breaking through bedrock with its steel horns.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "While seeking iron for food, it digs tunnels by breaking through bedrock with its steel horns.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "While seeking iron for food, it digs tunnels by breaking through bedrock with its steel horns.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "You can tell its age by the length of its iron horns. It claims an entire mountain as its territory.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "You can tell its age by the length of its iron horns. It claims an entire mountain as its territory.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "While seeking iron for food, it digs tunnels by breaking through bedrock with its steel horns.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "While seeking iron for food, it digs tunnels by breaking through bedrock with its steel horns.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "It claims an entire mountain as its own. The more wounds it has, the more it has battled, so don’t take it lightly.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It claims an entire mountain as its own. The more wounds it has, the more it has battled, so don’t take it lightly.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It claims an entire mountain as its own. The more wounds it has, the more it has battled, so don’t take it lightly.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "While seeking iron for food, it digs tunnels by breaking through bedrock with its steel horns.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aggron claims an entire mountain as its own territory. It mercilessly beats up anything that violates its environment. This Pokémon vigilantly patrols its territory at all times.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aggron is protective of its environment. If its mountain is ravaged by a landslide or a fire, this Pokémon will haul topsoil to the area, plant trees, and beautifully restore its own territory.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aggron has a horn sharp enough to perforate thick iron sheets. It brings down its opponents by ramming into them horn first.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Long ago, there was a king who wore a helmet meant to resemble the head of an Aggron. He was trying to channel the Pokémon’s strength.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
